<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean bond market closed for public holiday.</title>
<headline>South Korean bond market closed for public holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's bond market is closed on Wednesday for Buddha's Birthday, reopening Thursday.</p>
<p>Yields on benchmark three-year corporate bonds ended Tuesday higher due to weak demand despite relatively few new issues.</p>
<p>The yields ended at 12.30 percent, against the previous day's closing rate of 12.28 percent.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
